      "story_intro": "旧烽火楼的每一扇窗都是一只不肯闭上的眼睛：夜巡用它考『立体之守』——寒流从窗棂、屋脊与楼梯三向灌入，而双径其实只是楼里两条最长的窗。艾吉上楼那晚明白了一件事：塔阵守不住楼，是楼在人心里。",
      "story_intro_en": "In the old beacon tower every window is an eye that refuses to close: the watch used it to test three-dimensional keeping — the cold poured in through lattice, ridge and stair, while the twin lanes were only the tower's two longest windows. The night Eggy climbed it, the lesson arrived: the towers do not hold the house; the house holds when someone holds it.",
      "story_outro": "天亮清点，千窗无一盏熄灭。楼灵在门楣上落灰成字：最后一烽，极夜归营。",
      "story_outro_en": "At dawn's roll-call not one of the thousand windows had gone dark. The house spirit wrote in dust across the lintel: last beacon — the Homecoming of the Polar Night."
    },
